[stderr] +---
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Define original semantic tokens for typography, spacing, focus, motion, touch
[stderr] +targets, status, contrast, and non-colour cues. The contract enables later
[stderr] +responsive web UI and inherited PWA UI without selecting final visual assets or
[stderr] +numeric design decisions that remain gated.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependencies
[stderr] +
[stderr] +R0001 and R0002 are implementation dependencies. Retain GATE-0002 and
[stderr] +GATE-0004 for numeric contrast, font, and breakpoint claims; neither gate
[stderr] +blocks authoring this bounded token contract.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `src/app/design/tokens/` and the semantic token inventory.
[stderr] +- `docs/design-tokens.md` and `tests/app/design-tokens.*`.
[stderr] +- The token consumption contract used by shared UI, web, and PWA adapters.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Use semantic names such as surface, text, action, status, focus, spacing,
[stderr] +typography, motion, and target-size rather than screen- or asset-specific
[stderr] +values. Require visible focus, text-plus-shape/icon status cues, and
[stderr] +reduced-motion values that remove nonessential motion. Support scalable text,
[stderr] +semantic labels, and non-colour state indication without binding tokens to a
[stderr] +specific component or final visual composition.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Web UI consumes the shared semantic contract across responsive layouts. The
[stderr] +installed PWA inherits those tokens and accessibility behaviour; installation,
[stderr] +cache, and display-mode adaptation do not introduce a separate token system.
[stderr] +No final breakpoint or browser/device compatibility claim is made.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Non-goals
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Do not build screens, maps, layouts, final breakpoints, final artwork, fonts,
[stderr] +icons, audio, animations, or copied reference styling. Do not approve numeric
[stderr] +contrast, font, or breakpoint values while GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 remain
[stderr] +unresolved.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Asset assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`. This semantic contract explicitly
[stderr] +prohibits incidental asset creation: no final art, fonts, icons, audio, maps,
[stderr] +or other product assets may be created or reserved.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Verification
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Validate representative token fixtures contain semantic labels and
[stderr] +  text/non-colour cues for status.
[stderr] +- Validate reduced-motion values remove nonessential transitions without
[stderr] +  suppressing essential information.
[stderr] +- Confirm focus, target-size, typography, spacing, and status tokens are
[stderr] +  semantic and do not encode a screen or final asset.
[stderr] +- Record GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 as retained before any numeric design,
[stderr] +  contrast, font, or breakpoint claim.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Evidence
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Preserve token-validation results, representative non-colour and
[stderr] +reduced-motion fixtures, and the explicit retained-gate record.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Semantic tokens provide non-colour cues and reduced-motion values.
[stderr] +- The token contract can be consumed by web and PWA UI without platform forks.
[stderr] +- No final visual assets or approval-gated numeric claims are introduced.
