## Objective

Create only `../runbooks/R0002.md`, `../runbooks/R0003.md`, and
`../runbooks/R0010.md` for B0002. They map respectively to IMP-0002, IMP-0003,
and IMP-0010. B0001/R0001 is an implementation dependency, not an authoring
prerequisite: create these bounded contracts now even if R0001 has not yet run
or GATE-0001 remains unresolved.

## Context packet

Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0002 manifest record, its three catalogue
records, and only these specification sections: `03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,
`03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency`,
`04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour`, and
`04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy`.

## Output list

- `../runbooks/R0002.md` — IMP-0002; dependencies R0001.
- `../runbooks/R0003.md` — IMP-0003; dependencies R0001,R0002.
- `../runbooks/R0010.md` — IMP-0010; dependencies R0001,R0002.

## Required authoring content

For each output, use standard Supervisor front matter and the exact manifest
provenance (`source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch:
B0002`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`) plus `asset_impact:
not_applicable` and blank `asset_ids`, plus `audio_impact: not_applicable`,
blank `audio_ids`, `audio_brief`, and `audio_style_version`,
`audio_duration_seconds: 0`, and `audio_loop: not_applicable`. Make each an individually implementable
task containing objective, dependencies, relevant requirements, ownership,
behaviour, non-goals, web/PWA differences, verification/evidence, observable
acceptance criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` that prohibits incidental
assets.

## Validation procedure

Refuse a conflicting existing R ID or path. Load every output, compare all
metadata and dependencies to the manifest, verify provenance fields are
non-empty, and verify that all three outputs have the required sections.

## Checkpoint and update procedure

Update only B0002's checkpoint/state after all three outputs validate. Preserve
accepted outputs and repair only the failed assigned file on resume.

## Stop condition

Stop after these three files; do not resolve the retained design gates or write another R-series contract.

An unresolved R dependency or retained gate blocks later implementation only;
it must not block authoring and validating these three R contracts.

## Acceptance criteria

- R0002, R0003, and R0010 are the only outputs and each maps to its assigned IMP record.
- Each output is bounded, traceable, dependency-correct, and explicitly prohibits incidental asset work.
- Metadata, required sections, and manifest ownership are structurally validated before checkpointing.
- ID or ownership mismatches stop the batch without overwrite or renumbering.
