urned\n+  state/event rendering.\n+- Record the selected enforcement mechanism only after the retained GATE-0001\n+  tool decision; do not claim that gate is resolved here.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Preserve the dependency-rule test result, the fixture-adapter result, and an\n+architecture document showing the one-way core/adapter boundary.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Forbidden imports into the core are rejected.\n+- A fixture adapter can submit commands and consume returned state/events\n+  without directly mutating campaign state.\n+- The shared contract remains usable by web and PWA adapters without choosing\n+  implementation tooling or creating product assets.\ndiff --git a/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0003.md b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0003.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..ed4ec63625bd291fdda54b60ee00ea2eb819fff8\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0003.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,96 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0003\n+sequence: 3\n+title: Create deterministic test and fixture harness\n+dependencies:\n+  - R0001\n+  - R0002\n+requirement_ids:\n+  - NFR-0010\n+  - NFR-0012\n+source_specifications:\n+  - specification/03-technical-contract.md#observability-quality-evidence-and-release-verification\n+source_catalogue_ids:\n+  - IMP-0003\n+authoring_batch: B0002\n+factory_stages:\n+  - F011\n+  - F012\n+  - F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; fixtures use non-product deterministic data.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Establish layered unit, content, integration, and reserved browser-test\n+conventions with isolated RNG, clock, and persistence fixtures. The harness\n+must be repeatable and must never access real services or player data.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0001 and R0002 are implementation dependencies. This contract may be authored\n+and structurally validated before they run; its later implementation uses the\n+shared seam from R0002.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- Test-runner configuration and `tests/{core,content,platform,app}/fixtures`.\n+- Deterministic fixture factories plus fake clock and RNG interfaces.\n+- `docs/testing.md` and the reserved browser-test convention.\n+\n+## Behaviour\n+\n+Provide factories that receive controlled clock, RNG, and storage fakes, reset\n+their state between cases, and expose explicit deterministic inputs. Define\n+separate layers for core, content, platform, and application checks so future\n+features add evidence at the appropriate layer instead of coupling tests to\n+real browser state or services.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Shared fixtures cover core behaviour. Web and PWA adapter tests use isolated\n+platform fakes; reserved browser tests are conventions only, not claims of a\n+real browser/device matrix. PWA cache and web origin storage remain distinct\n+from fixture storage.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not add final feature assertions, real browser or device compatibility\n+claims, production telemetry, network calls, player data, campaign content, or\n+product assets. Do not create incidental art, fonts, icons, audio, maps, or\n+reference-derived fixture content.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`. Fixtures contain only deterministic,\n+non-product data and must not create incidental product assets or reserve them.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Run a representative core fixture repeatedly and prove identical results.\n+- Deliberately fail a fixture assertion and prove the runner reports it.\n+- Verify fixture storage is isolated from browser-origin and production data.\n+- Retain GATE-0002: this harness does not establish compatibility or\n+  performance claims.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Record repeated-run output, the deliberate-failure detection result, and an\n+isolation check showing no real service, player, or browser-origin storage use.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Repeated execution of a controlled fixture returns identical results.\n+- Fixture state, clock, RNG, and storage are isolated and resettable.\n+- The harness defines layered conventions without asserting final features,\n+  browser/device support, or production telemetry.\ndiff --git a/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0010.md b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0010.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..6e68f45d14d44df389f1348a4e7ac2851ef5c887\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0010.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,104 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0010\n+sequence: 10\n+title: Establish semantic accessibility design tokens\n+dependencies:\n+  - R0001\n+  - R0002\n+requirement_ids:\n+  - REQ-0007\n+  - REQ-0010\n+  - NFR-0004\n+  - NFR-0008\n+source_specifications:\n+  - specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\n+  - specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\n+source_catalogue_ids:\n+  - IMP-0010\n+authoring_batch: B0002\n+factory_stages:\n+  - F011\n+  - F012\n+  - F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No final artwork, fonts, or icons; semantic tokens only and prohibit incidental assets.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define original semantic tokens for typography, spacing, focus, motion, touch\n+targets, status, contrast, and non-colour cues. The contract enables later\n+responsive web UI and inherited PWA UI without selecting final visual assets or\n+numeric design decisions that remain gated.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0001 and R0002 are implementation dependencies. Retain GATE-0002 and\n+GATE-0004 for numeric contrast, font, and breakpoint claims; neither gate\n+blocks authoring this bounded token contract.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/app/design/tokens/` and the semantic token inventory.\n+- `docs/design-tokens.md` and `tests/app/design-tokens.*`.\n+- The token consumption contract used by shared UI, web, and PWA adapters.\n+\n+## Behaviour\n+\n+Use semantic names such as surface, text, action, status, focus, spacing,\n+typography, motion, and target-size rather than screen- or asset-specific\n+values. Require visible focus, text-plus-shape/icon status cues, and\n+reduced-motion values that remove nonessential motion. Support scalable text,\n+semantic labels, and non-colour state indication without binding tokens to a\n+specific component or final visual composition.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web UI consumes the shared semantic contract across responsive layouts. The\n+installed PWA inherits those tokens and accessibility behaviour; installation,\n+cache, and display-mode adaptation do not introduce a separate token system.\n+No final breakpoint or browser/device compatibility claim is made.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not build screens, maps, layouts, final breakpoints, final artwork, fonts,\n+icons, audio, animations, or copied reference styling. Do not approve numeric\n+contrast, font, or breakpoint values while GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 remain\n+unresolved.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`. This semantic contract explicitly\n+prohibits incidental asset creation: no final art, fonts, icons, audio, maps,\n+or other product assets may be created or reserved.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Validate representative token fixtures contain semantic labels and\n+  text/non-colour cues for status.\n+- Validate reduced-motion values remove nonessential transitions without\n+  suppressing essential information.\n+- Confirm focus, target-size, typography, spacing, and status tokens are\n+  semantic and do not encode a screen or final asset.\n+- Record GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 as retained before any numeric design,\n+  contrast, font, or breakpoint claim.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Preserve token-validation results, representative non-colour and\n+reduced-motion fixtures, and the explicit retained-gate record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Semantic tokens provide non-colour cues and reduced-motion values.\n+- The token contract can be consumed by web and PWA UI without platform forks.\n+- No final visual assets or approval-gated numeric claims are introduced.\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"node - <<'NODE'\nconst fs=require('fs');\nconst root='projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4';\nconst manifest=require('./'+root+'/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json');\nconst catalogue=require('./'+root+'/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json');\nconst targets=['R0002','R0003','R0010'];\nconst required=['Objective','Dependencies','Ownership','Behaviour','Web and PWA differences','Non-goals','Asset assessment','Verification','Evidence','Acceptance criteria'];\nfunction fm(text){const end=text.indexOf('\\\\n---',4); if(\"'!text.startsWith('\"'---\\\\n')||end<0) throw Error('invalid front matter'); const out={}, lines=text.slice(4,end).split('\\\\n'); let k; for(const line of lines){if(/\"'^  - /.test(line)&&k) (out[k]??=[]).push(line.slice(4)); else {const p=line.indexOf('\"':'); if(p>=0){k=line.slice(0,p); const v=line.slice(p+1).trim(); out[k]=v||[];}}} return out;}\nfor(const id of targets){ const m=manifest.r_contracts.find(x=>x.id===id); if(\"'!m) throw Error(id+'\"' missing manifest'); const c=catalogue.contracts.find(x=>x.id===m.catalogue_id); const path=root+'/runbooks/'+id+'.md'; if(\"'!fs.existsSync(path)) throw Error(id+'\"' missing output'); const text=fs.readFileSync(path,'utf8'), meta=fm(text); const same=(a,b)=>JSON.stringify(a)===JSON.stringify(b); fo